{
    "word": "horsepower",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "77bd43a3-5301-3826-a09e-f7a421439ecd",
                "word": "horsepower",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "828da968-3352-4574-bb93-83b1646cf121",
                        "entry_id": "77bd43a3-5301-3826-a09e-f7a421439ecd",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "horsepowers"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "c6f8355e-8c6f-4fc2-bb1a-a7d4bdbd89f6",
                        "entry_id": "77bd43a3-5301-3826-a09e-f7a421439ecd",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "horsepower"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f222ecf7-bde7-3cce-988b-832c2fe5d664",
                        "entry_id": "77bd43a3-5301-3826-a09e-f7a421439ecd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Power derived from the motion of a horse."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "literally",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1f7b6391-7621-4fcb-a25a-f52f21f9c12e",
                                "sense_id": "f222ecf7-bde7-3cce-988b-832c2fe5d664",
                                "text": "Shillibeer's bus came in 1829 drawn by three horses. Later two horses were found sufficient to pull these closed wagonettes, which eventually had outside seats, and later on the substitution of a motor for horsepower."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4e426348-4513-4eb4-be40-fdf5f18ff1ba",
                                "sense_id": "f222ecf7-bde7-3cce-988b-832c2fe5d664",
                                "text": "The Sun Inn is an attractive black-and-white building, and has an old mounting block outside as a reminder of the days when horsepower meant four legs and a saddle."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "40ea6468-77ef-46c3-8b22-7b28e3fa6d3b",
                                "sense_id": "f222ecf7-bde7-3cce-988b-832c2fe5d664",
                                "text": "The wheel was to have been turned by horsepower, but it was adapted to be driven by a mill-wheel on the river Derwent […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5b2da96c-49e6-3ea5-97f3-ca98903a9262",
                        "entry_id": "77bd43a3-5301-3826-a09e-f7a421439ecd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A nonmetric unit of power with various definitions, commonly the mechanical horsepower, approximately equal to 745.7 watts."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bb80d48f-ca75-4942-9a56-ef1ea8483817",
                                "sense_id": "5b2da96c-49e6-3ea5-97f3-ca98903a9262",
                                "text": "Equally I can stand in a station like Lucerne in Switzerland, and watch with ill-concealed admiration the majestic entry of one of the latest Gotthard \"Ae 6/6\" electrics, packing 6,000 horsepower within its 60 ft. of length and 121 tons of weight, with its sleek dark green sides and handsome stainless steel bands and front wings."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e7e427ff-1e43-427b-bf6f-5352fb0a2473",
                                "sense_id": "5b2da96c-49e6-3ea5-97f3-ca98903a9262",
                                "text": "As Quincy recovered from our one-block adrenaline burst, I gunned all 700 horsepower once more. Even with the pedal to the metal, the Exelero's sheer bulk caused a multisecond lag from the twin-turbo-charged V12's wind-up to actual launch."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9203c31e-5529-4831-ab72-69afe8e62770",
                                "sense_id": "5b2da96c-49e6-3ea5-97f3-ca98903a9262",
                                "text": "In the past, before the widespread adoption of SI units, the work that engines were capable of doing was compared with the work that horses could do – hence the term ‘horsepower’. Various people came up with various equivalencies, but the modern agreed definition is that 1 horsepower is 746 joules per second or 746 watts."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d0b80666-63e7-376f-ab6f-284f895f5677",
                        "entry_id": "77bd43a3-5301-3826-a09e-f7a421439ecd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Metric horsepower, a metric unit approximately equal to 735.5 watts."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7d37c7e2-4fbd-3714-a5d4-e772df6b2104",
                        "entry_id": "77bd43a3-5301-3826-a09e-f7a421439ecd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Strength, performance capability, specs, or similar."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8e495c3f-5a58-47e1-8c62-88c953eb109f",
                                "sense_id": "7d37c7e2-4fbd-3714-a5d4-e772df6b2104",
                                "text": "political horsepower"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "deeb7501-74c6-4227-ba67-f21f34153864",
                                "sense_id": "7d37c7e2-4fbd-3714-a5d4-e772df6b2104",
                                "text": "My patron who sent this to me to do a whole video on, you know, Convergence or whatever, being able to use this as a desktop, uh, replacement, or at least a desktop type thing, it’s impossible for me, I can’t do it, this device just doesn’t have that type of horsepower even to run itself, let alone actually run desktop Linux, it just can’t do it, I haven’t figured out how to do it."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f02c2241-1709-4152-8467-b8c2b104e263",
